  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Boulenger's featherfin tetra, Bryconaethiops boulengeri, is a large alestid characin from the Congo river basin and Lake Tanganyika. Rarely imported, it is a peaceful shoaling species for a community of larger fish, and is farmed commercially for food in its native countries. It grows to 250 mm SL.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Native to the Congo river basin in Cameroon, Central African Republic, Democratic Republic of Congo, Republic of Congo and Zambia. It's also found in Lake Tanganyika.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Rivers and lakes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>An active species that needs a tank measuring at least 120 × 45 × 45 cm, about 243 litres.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>It requires a good flow of water through the tank, and decent oxygenation. The choice of decor isn't critical, but a substrate of sand with some driftwood branches, and perhaps some smooth rocks can look very effective. Try to leave as much open swimming space as possible.</p><ul><li>Needs strong current, with the filter turning the tank over 8–12 times an hour</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<ul><li>Temperature: 22–26°C</li><li>pH: 6.0–8.0</li><li>Hardness: 3–20 dGH</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Omnivorous. Offer a mixture of live, frozen and dried foods. Prawns and live earthworms are particularly relished.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Peaceful with anything that isn't too small as to be considered food. Best kept with other similarly-sized characins, robust cichlids, Loricariids and other bottom dwellers such as Polypterus species. It's a shoaling species so buy a group if possible.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Unknown.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>Unrecorded in the hobby.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "seriouslyfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.seriouslyfish.com/species/bryconaethiops-boulengeri",
      "html": "<p>This rarely imported species makes an attractive addition to a community of larger peaceful fish. It is farmed commercially for food in its native countries.</p>"
    }
  ],
